# GeneLabs CTI Workbench — Amazon Bedrock configuration
#
# Copy to  config/bedrock.env  and fill in. That file is gitignored: it holds
# credentials. Nothing else in the repository reads secrets.
#
# Load it with:
#   scripts\load_bedrock_env.ps1        (Windows, current PowerShell session)
#   source scripts/load_bedrock_env.sh  (macOS, Linux, WSL)
#
# The headless runner loads it automatically.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Route Claude Code at Bedrock
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK=1

# The region your Bedrock model access lives in.
AWS_REGION=us-west-2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Credentials — pick ONE of A, B or C
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# A. Bedrock API key. The simplest, and what you have if someone handed you
#    "a Claude API key for Bedrock". It is a bearer token scoped to Bedrock,
#    not an Anthropic key and not a full AWS key pair.
AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=

# B. IAM access key pair. Set AWS_SESSION_TOKEN too if these are temporary.
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=

# C. A named AWS profile, including SSO. Run `aws sso login --profile <name>`
#    first. Best option if GeneLabs federates AWS access through SSO.
# AWS_PROFILE=genelabs-bedrock

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Pin the models
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Always pin. Unpinned aliases resolve to Claude Code's built-in default for
# Bedrock, which may not be enabled in your account and may not be the model
# you intend to be billed for.
#
# The us. prefix is a cross-region inference profile. Use eu. or apac. for
# those geographies, us-gov. in GovCloud. Check what your account can actually
# invoke with:  aws bedrock list-inference-profiles --region $AWS_REGION

# Start with Opus. This task is judgment heavy and runs monthly.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=us.anthropic.claude-opus-5

# Background work: session titles and similar. Cheaper model, same account.
ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL=us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0

# If your account exposes models through an application inference profile
# instead, use its ARN as the model id:
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=arn:aws:bedrock:us-west-2:123456789012:application-inference-profile/cti-workbench

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Optional
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Prompt caching is not available in every Bedrock region. If cache token
# counts stay at zero, that is why, and every run costs full price.
# DISABLE_PROMPT_CACHING=1

# Service tier: default, flex or priority. Availability varies by model.
# ANTHROPIC_BEDROCK_SERVICE_TIER=default

# Route through a gateway rather than Bedrock directly.
# ANTHROPIC_BEDROCK_BASE_URL=https://bedrock-runtime.us-west-2.amazonaws.com

# Bedrock Guardrails, if GeneLabs requires content filtering on model traffic.
# ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_HEADERS=X-Amzn-Bedrock-GuardrailIdentifier: <id>\nX-Amzn-Bedrock-GuardrailVersion: 1
